{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "laplace_beltrami_band_mms",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady metric spherical Laplacian (Laplace-Beltrami) diffusion on a REGIONAL latlon band lat in [30,60] deg (strictly inside (-90,90), so cos phi>0 -- the pole singularity 1/cos^2(+-90) is avoided; the GLOBAL pole-cap Laplacian is a documented FOLLOW-UP), periodic in longitude over the full zonal circle (lon0_deg=0, dlon_deg=360/NLON). u_t = kappa (laplacian(u) - Lstar), laplacian lowered by grids/latlon/rules/laplace_beltrami_lon_periodic_lat_zero_grad (periodic zonal wrap + zero-gradient Neumann band edges, cos(lat)-weighted mimetic FV). Manufactured STEADY solution u*(lon,lat) = cos^4(s) cos(2 lambda), lambda=(pi/180)lon, s=(pi/2)(phi-phi_mid)/B, phi=(pi/180)lat, phi_mid=(pi/180)45, B=(pi/180)15 -- a pole-cap-style profile REMAPPED so the band edges lat=30 and lat=60 play the role of the poles: F=cos^4(s) has F,F',F'',F''' all vanishing at s=+-pi/2 (the edges), making u* supercompatible with the rule's zero-flux Neumann faces to O(dlat_deg^2) (a plain non-vanishing-derivative field would collapse the meridional pole-face order to 1, the same node-coincident-boundary degradation problems/latlon_diffusion_meridional_zero_grad documents). The zonal factor cos(2 lambda) is smooth and periodic, so the (180/pi)^2/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi) zonal metric weight is genuinely exercised (both Laplacian terms active, unlike the meridional-only per-degree companion). The manufactured Laplace-Beltrami Lstar = cos(2 lambda) [ (-sin phi F'(phi) + cos phi F''(phi)) /(R_sphere^2 cos phi) - 4 F(phi)/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi) ] (F'(phi)=-4 cos^3 s sin s (pi/2)/B, F''(phi)=(12 cos^2 s sin^2 s - 4 cos^4 s)((pi/2)/B)^2) is the exact steady source, so u_t=kappa(laplacian(u*)-Lstar)=0 continuously and the discrete field drifts only by the spatial truncation -- what the assertions and the convergence sweep measure. GRID CONTRACT (grids/latlon/grid.esm): R_sphere=2 (m, test value baked into Lstar as a literal), lat0_deg=30, dlon_deg=360/NLON, dlat_deg=30/(NLAT-1) as observeds using the metaparameter NAMES (substituted as integer literals at load per esm-spec 9.7.6, so the loader-API convergence sweep keeps the geometry consistent). BOTH NLON and NLAT stay OPEN (defaults 144 x 91) and refine together in the sweep (n=NLON=NLAT-1, dphi and dlambda halve together). The ic, Lstar, and reference INLINE the grid coordinates from literals + the metaparameter names (never the free-name lat_coord/coslat templates), because free-name geometry is out of scope in the bindings' build-time cellwise evaluator (esm-spec build-time caveat; same pattern as latlon_diffusion_meridional_zero_grad). ERROR MODEL: at kappa=1, T=0.5 the truncation-driven relative-L2 drift is O(h^2); at the default NLON=144,NLAT=91 it is 4.9e-4 (Linf 5.6e-4), and the NLON/NLAT = 16/32/64/128 (paired 17/33/65/129) sweep gives 2.64e-2 / 6.65e-3 / 1.67e-3 / ~4.2e-4 (observed order ~2 in L2 and Linf); exact per-resolution values are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/laplace_beltrami_band_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon",
      "equation:laplacian",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Williamson, D. L., Drake, J. B., Hack, J. J., Jakob, R., & Swarztrauber, P. N. (1992). A standard test set for numerical approximations to the shallow water equations in spherical geometry. Journal of Computational Physics, 102(1), 211-224. (Laplace-Beltrami on the sphere; latitude-longitude pole context.)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "LaplaceBeltramiBand": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon/rules/laplace_beltrami_lon_periodic_lat_zero_grad.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Diffused scalar over the lon x lat index sets on the regional band."
        },
        "kappa": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant diffusivity; the forced-steady balance u_t = kappa (laplacian(u) - Lstar) = 0 holds for any value, so it only sets the time scale."
        },
        "R_sphere": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 2.0,
          "description": "Sphere radius (test value); the rule's free name for the metric 1/R_sphere^2 factor. Baked as the literal 2 inside Lstar so the manufactured source matches the discretized operator."
        },
        "lat0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 30.0,
          "description": "Band's southern edge latitude (=30); the grid's lat0_deg free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract)."
        },
        "dlon_deg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "description": "Zonal spacing 360/NLON (full periodic circle); NLON is the document metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6) so the sweep keeps dlon_deg consistent."
        },
        "dlat_deg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "deg",
          "description": "Meridional spacing (60-30)/(NLAT-1) over the band; NLAT is the document metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load."
        },
        "Lstar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Analytic Laplace-Beltrami of u* = cos^4(s) cos(2 lambda) (the exact steady source; derivation in metadata.description). Constant in time; kappa (laplacian(u) - Lstar) is the residual that holds u* steady."
        }
      },
